meta {
  name: Invalid Avatar Key (400)
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/users/me
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "avatarKey": "avatars/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/9f54a22a-2c65-4de5-b224-f1b5def25656.jpg"
  }
}

docs {
  A well-formed key that belongs to a DIFFERENT user. Expect 400
  {"error": "Invalid avatar key"}.

  This is the check that stops the avatar field from becoming a way to point
  at any object in the bucket. The key is just a string the client sends, so
  the server re-derives ownership from the user id embedded in the path rather
  than trusting it.

  Also rejected: path traversal, a non-uuid filename, a .png extension, and
  anything with extra path segments before or after the expected shape.
}
